WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.375
<b>In previous verses,</b>

2
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:48.625
<b>Lord Krishna explained</b>

3
00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:53.916
<b>that to keep life free from sin, </b>
<b>renouncing selfishness is essential. </b>

4
00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:56.458
<b>According to Vedic systems,</b>

5
00:00:56.458 --> 00:01:01.125
<b>performing yajna (sacrifice) or </b>
<b>offering duties as oblations is necessary.</b>

6
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:06.625
<b>Such karma yoga (path of action) </b>
<b>is the way to purify the mind.</b>

7
00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:13.125
<b>In these two verses, Krishna describes</b>
<b>the person whose mind is pure,</b>

8
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:15.750
<b>who has renounced selfishness,</b>

9
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.375
<b>and harbors no desire for pleasure or indulgence.</b>

10
00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:26.500
<b>In these verses,</b>

11
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.875
<b>Krishna speaks of one who is self-content,</b>

12
00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:36.458
<b>joyful, and free from material desires.</b>

13
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:39.375
<b>Such a person's mind is pure,</b>

14
00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:46.000
<b>and they perform no action </b>
<b>driven by wants or cravings.</b>

15
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.916
<b>But this raises a question –</b>

16
00:01:47.916 --> 00:01:51.291
<b>why does such a person act at all?</b>

17
00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:54.750
<b>And why are they free from material desires?</b>

18
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.708
<b>The answer to both is single:</b>

19
00:01:57.708 --> 00:01:59.416
<b>Joy.</b>

20
00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:03.875
<b>For such individuals, performing action</b>
<b>is a joyous process,</b>

21
00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:08.375
<b>a process through which</b>
<b>they understand their soul.</b>

22
00:02:08.375 --> 00:02:15.583
<b>This process is so blissful that it hardly</b>
<b>feels like duty or action at all.</b>

23
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:20.791
<b>Ordinarily, humans perform </b>
<b>duties for only two reasons:</b>

24
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:21.708
<b>One,</b>

25
00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.875
<b>to fulfill some desire</b>

26
00:02:23.875 --> 00:02:25.083
<b>and second,</b>

27
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:28.000
<b>to meet some obligation.</b>

28
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.833
<b>But one who has delved deep into spirituality</b>

29
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:40.750
<b>and developed their spiritual form no longer has </b>
<b>such desires or obligations driving their actions.</b>

30
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.375
<b>They still act,</b>

31
00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:44.416
<b>but selflessly.</b>

32
00:02:44.416 --> 00:02:45.708
<b>For welfare.</b>

33
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:47.791
<b>With the spirit of helping others.</b>

34
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:48.958
<b>Yet even here,</b>

35
00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:54.541
<b>their focus remains solely on </b>
<b>performing the action, not on its results.</b>

36
00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.875
<b>Such individuals have no compulsions.</b>

37
00:02:57.875 --> 00:03:00.416
<b>They expect nothing from the world,</b>

38
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:05.375
<b>and therefore have no commitments to it.</b>

39
00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:06.000
<b>Now,</b>

40
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.166
<b>a question might arise –</b>

41
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:12.833
<b>if such people have no commitment to the world,</b>

42
00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:18.833
<b>what necessitates their selfless actions?</b>

43
00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:21.958
<b>The answer lies in the verses that follow.</b>

44
00:03:26.416 --> 00:03:30.375
<b>Perhaps you too experience moments</b>

45
00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:37.625
<b>when duties feel like an </b>
<b>overwhelming burden, shackling you down,</b>

46
00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:44.875
<b>while your mind struggles to </b>
<b>find freedom from this weight.</b>

47
00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:47.958
<b>Everyone yearns for such freedom,</b>

48
00:03:47.958 --> 00:03:50.625
<b>but how is it attained?</b>

49
00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:53.875
<b>Who is worthy of this freedom?</b>

50
00:03:53.875 --> 00:03:56.541
<b>One who is surrounded by desires,</b>

51
00:03:56.541 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>who expects much from this world,</b>

52
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:03.541
<b>remains bound, doesn't they?</b>

53
00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:06.541
<b>Where there are desires and expectations,</b>

54
00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:15.125
<b>one must bear the constraints of </b>
<b>duties and responsibilities to fulfill them.</b>

55
00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:19.958
<b>But if you truly wish to be free,</b>

56
00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:23.916
<b>you must elevate your spiritual consciousness.</b>

57
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:26.416
<b>Only when one performs actions</b>

58
00:04:26.416 --> 00:04:34.416
<b>without desiring specific </b>
<b>outcomes can they truly be free.</b>

59
00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:38.208
<b>Then no responsibility feels like a burden.</b>

60
00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:42.541
<b>How to begin this journey?</b>

61
00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:44.666
<b>Through contentment.</b>

62
00:04:44.666 --> 00:04:47.625
<b>Practice being content in life.</b>

63
00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:55.375
<b>Instead of striving for what you don't have, </b>
<b>increase your gratitude for what you do have.</b>

64
00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:56.958
<b>Remember</b>

65
00:04:56.958 --> 00:05:03.250
<b>those moments when you dreamed </b>
<b>of reaching your current state,</b>

66
00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:07.083
<b>when you yearned for what is now your present.</b>

67
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:14.416
<b>Then consider how many times </b>
<b>this has happened in life.</b>

68
00:05:14.416 --> 00:05:20.250
<b>When you received what you wanted,</b>

69
00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:25.666
<b>when you thought that obtaining </b>
<b>something would bring satisfaction.</b>

70
00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:27.041
<b>But</b>

71
00:05:27.041 --> 00:05:30.750
<b>did satisfaction come?</b>

72
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.791
<b>No, right?</b>

73
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:37.041
<b>This chase after mirages continues even now.</b>

74
00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:43.958
<b>Then you'll realize that satisfaction cannot </b>
<b>be obtained merely through material pleasures.</b>

75
00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:48.916
<b>Contentment and happiness are states of mind.</b>

76
00:05:48.916 --> 00:05:53.291
<b>They must be practiced to be attained.</b>

77
00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:54.708
<b>Regular spiritual practice,</b>

78
00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:55.958
<b>self-reflection,</b>

79
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:58.666
<b>and spiritual study –</b>

80
00:05:58.666 --> 00:06:03.541
<b>these will help you attain this life contentment.</b>

81
00:06:03.541 --> 00:06:04.583
<b>And</b>

82
00:06:04.583 --> 00:06:07.666
<b>if you learn to remain content in life,</b>

83
00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:15.625
<b>know that you're progressing </b>
<b>toward spiritual satisfaction as well.</b>

84
00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:24.583
<b>How sweet is the love between </b>
<b>parents and children.</b>

85
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:26.958
<b>Because there's no selfishness here.</b>

86
00:06:26.958 --> 00:06:28.166
<b>Parents</b>

87
00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:34.458
<b>continuously do everything for their </b>
<b>children without expecting any praise.</b>

88
00:06:34.458 --> 00:06:35.500
<b> Similarly,</b>

89
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.625
<b>consider those siblings.</b>

90
00:06:37.625 --> 00:06:42.916
<b>Why are their relationships so sweet?</b>

91
00:06:42.916 --> 00:06:45.791
<b>Because there are no expectations,</b>

92
00:06:45.791 --> 00:06:51.625
<b>only an effort to help one another.</b>

93
00:06:51.625 --> 00:06:55.833
<b>Whether relationships are familial or social,</b>

94
00:06:55.833 --> 00:07:00.166
<b>their sweetness is founded on selflessness.</b>

95
00:07:00.166 --> 00:07:02.458
<b>But</b>

96
00:07:02.458 --> 00:07:06.208
<b> here, humans make one error.</b>

97
00:07:06.208 --> 00:07:10.291
<b>They wait for others to take initiative.</b>

98
00:07:10.291 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>They think they'll help when others </b>
<b>show selflessness toward them.</b>

99
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:19.333
<b>But</b>

100
00:07:19.333 --> 00:07:21.500
<b>isn't this just transaction?</b>

101
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.083
<b>Like some business.</b>

102
00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:26.333
<b>This isn't relationship.</b>

103
00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:29.375
<b>Practice taking initiative.</b>

104
00:07:29.375 --> 00:07:35.833
<b>Try helping others without </b>
<b>expecting anything in return.</b>

105
00:07:35.833 --> 00:07:37.125
<b>Then see,</b>

106
00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:40.541
<b>not only will you experience infinite satisfaction,</b>

107
00:07:40.541 --> 00:07:41.416
<b>but</b>

108
00:07:41.416 --> 00:07:46.333
<b>soon your relationships will</b>
<b>begin to sparkle with new joy.</b>

109
00:07:46.333 --> 00:07:53.000
<b>If even a few people adopt this mindset, </b>
<b>relationships will strengthen,</b>

110
00:07:53.000 --> 00:08:00.583
<b>spiritual progress will be encouraged, </b>
<b>and a supportive society will emerge.</b>

111
00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:07.916
<b>Don't wait for others. Take the initiative yourself.</b>

112
00:08:07.916 --> 00:08:09.791
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

113
00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:15.750
<b>Self-reliance</b>

114
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.416
<b>and self-satisfaction,</b>

115
00:08:18.416 --> 00:08:25.625
<b>try applying these two principles</b>
<b>in your professional life.</b>

116
00:08:25.625 --> 00:08:26.791
<b>But</b>

117
00:08:26.791 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>how to do this?</b>

118
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:33.250
<b>Some self-reflection is necessary.</b>

119
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.208
<b>Think about it.</b>

120
00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:41.291
<b>Is others' approval or their praise even necessary?</b>

121
00:08:41.291 --> 00:08:48.166
<b>Depending on others' praise is inviting </b>
<b>frustration into your life, isn't it?</b>

122
00:08:48.166 --> 00:08:49.250
<b>But</b>

123
00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.583
<b>this question naturally arises –</b>

124
00:08:52.583 --> 00:09:00.750
<b>in professional life, progress depends </b>
<b>on approval from those in higher positions.</b>

125
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:05.583
<b>So isn't their perspective necessary?</b>

126
00:09:05.583 --> 00:09:07.166
<b>The question is valid.</b>

127
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:09.083
<b>And the answer is</b>

128
00:09:09.083 --> 00:09:10.416
<b>yes.</b>

129
00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:16.375
<b>Perhaps pleasing senior officials is necessary.</b>

130
00:09:16.375 --> 00:09:17.208
<b>But</b>

131
00:09:17.208 --> 00:09:23.708
<b>they too will only appreciate </b>
<b>work that's beautifully accomplished.</b>

132
00:09:23.708 --> 00:09:25.166
<b>Therefore,</b>

133
00:09:25.166 --> 00:09:32.291
<b>focus only on work quality, on your efforts.</b>

134
00:09:32.291 --> 00:09:39.541
<b>If while working, you remain constantly </b>
<b>gripped by various thoughts and worries,</b>

135
00:09:39.541 --> 00:09:41.583
<b>thinking about </b>

136
00:09:41.583 --> 00:09:46.958
<b>who will like the work and who won't,</b>

137
00:09:46.958 --> 00:09:51.791
<b>can that work be done with complete efficiency?</b>

138
00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:53.333
<b>No, right?</b>

139
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:54.583
<b>Understand</b>

140
00:09:54.583 --> 00:09:57.791
<b>what your senior officials want,</b>

141
00:09:57.791 --> 00:10:02.083
<b>plan your work accordingly.</b>

142
00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:05.291
<b>But once work begins,</b>

143
00:10:05.291 --> 00:10:10.166
<b>then focus solely and completely on it,</b>

144
00:10:10.166 --> 00:10:14.625
<b>not on whether it will be praised or not.</b>

145
00:10:14.625 --> 00:10:17.750
<b>Success is like a butterfly –</b>

146
00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:24.041
<b>if you chase it, perhaps you'll be able to catch it,</b>

147
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:26.166
<b>perhaps not.</b>

148
00:10:26.166 --> 00:10:32.125
<b>But if you've worked to grow many</b>
<b>beautiful flowers in your life,</b>

149
00:10:32.125 --> 00:10:41.208
<b>their fragrance will naturally attract not one </b>
<b>but many butterflies to your life's garden.</b>

150
00:10:41.208 --> 00:10:43.708
<b>Professional life is just the same.</b>

151
00:10:43.708 --> 00:10:47.625
<b>If you've focused only on growing flowers,</b>

152
00:10:47.625 --> 00:10:53.458
<b>meaning skillfully completing your work,</b>

153
00:10:53.458 --> 00:11:00.250
<b>then success's butterfly will naturally </b>
<b>be attracted and come to you.</b>

154
00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.916
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

